  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CHAI- Sustainable HIV/AIDS and Health Financing II - CHAI- sustainable HIV/AIDS and Health Financing</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">CHAI- h&#xe5;llbar hiv/aids och h&#xe4;lsofinansiering II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">- The overall outcome is the number of participating countries implementing equitable health financing strategies through an inclusive process as indicated by analysis on implications on human rights, gender, and access to care.- Overarching Vision for 2017: A regional network of countries who have gained the independence and ability to more efficiently, transparently and accountably manage and direct health resources.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen syftar till att bidra till en h&#xe5;llbar h&#xe4;lsofinansiering i &#xe5;tta l&#xe4;nder &#x2013; Sydafrika, Swaziland, Zimbabwe, Malawi, Zambia, Kamerun, Rwanda och Etiopien. Fr&#xe5;n visionen med ett regionalt n&#xe4;tverk av l&#xe4;nder som effektivt, transparant och ansvarsfullt kan hantera och styra resurser f&#xf6;r h&#xe4;lsa f&#xf6;r alla syftar programmet till att; (i) institutionalisera h&#xe4;lsofinansieringsstrategier och reformer; (ii) f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra och integrera (s&#xe5;v&#xe4;l verksamhetsm&#xe4;ssiga som ekonomiadministrativa) informationssystem f&#xf6;r evidensbaserade beslut, samt att (iii) st&#xe4;rka delaktighet och &#xe4;garskap genom kapacitetsuppbyggnad och verktygsutveckling. Det regionala perspektivet &#xe4;r att bidra erfarenhetsutbyte och till skapandet av kanaler f&#xf6;r erfarenhetsutbyte och samr&#xe5;d, fr&#xe4;mst genom redan etablerade kanaler som de regionala organisationerna. Projektperioden &#xe4;r 1 April 2014 till 31 december 2017. 
 
Projektet &#xe4;r ber&#xe4;ttigat d&#xe5; m&#xe5;nga l&#xe4;nder f n arbetar med att reformera sina system f&#xf6;r h&#xe4;lsofinansiering, vilket ger m&#xf6;jligheter att p&#xe5;verka den framtida utformningen f&#xf6;r f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad tillg&#xe4;nglighet p&#xe5; lika villkor och f&#xf6;r r&#xe4;ttvisa finansieringsl&#xf6;sningar. M&#xe5;nga l&#xe4;nder har dessutom sv&#xe5;righeter att m&#xf6;ta kraven fr&#xe5;n finansi&#xe4;rer p&#xe5; resultatorientering och rapportering, vilket dels p&#xe5;verkar m&#xf6;jligheterna att f&#xe5; extern finansiering, dels f&#xf6;ruts&#xe4;ttningarna f&#xf6;r ett effektivt resursutnyttjande. St&#xf6;det fr&#xe5;n CHAI n&#xe4;r det g&#xe4;ller informationssystem syftar d&#xe4;rf&#xf6;r till att st&#xe4;rka de nationella systemen f&#xf6;r att kunna leva upp till dessa krav.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contribution aims to contribute to sustainable health financing in 8 countries; South Africa, Swaziland, Zimbabwe, Malawi, Zambia, Cameroon, Rwanda and Ethiopia. With a vision to create &#x201c;a regional network of countries who have gained the independence and ability to more efficiently, transparently and accountably manage and direct health resources&#x201d; the project aims to (i) support implementation and institutionalization of  health financing strategies and other high impact reforms by iteratively moving plans to action; (ii) strengthen management accounting systems to enable country governments to gain greater control over key aspects of health sector financing, and (iii) empower Governments with tools, skills and processes that will provide capacity to manage an increasing share of domestic resources allocated to healthcare.

The project is merited as many countries are in the process to reform their systems for financing health services, which provides an opportunity to support a process towards equity in access and fairness in financing. Second, many countries, both those who support external financing and those providing external support are challenged by the increasing demands for accountability and performance reporting. The support provided by CHAI in developing coherent management accounting systems integrating performance or management information with financial information, aims at strengthening government systems to enable them to deliver on reporting on both accountability and operational results.</narrative>
  </description>
